WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:06.204
Your agent builds great pages. Pages turns each one into a link.

00:07.000 --> 00:13.504
Ask your agent for an interactive page. It writes the files, and checks them against the rules.

00:14.800 --> 00:18.928
It's a real page, with its own scripts and its own data.

00:22.900 --> 00:30.964
Now publish it. Pages opens a pull request from your fork, checks every file, and puts the space on its own branch.

00:32.600 --> 00:37.256
No new account, and no keys. Just GitHub, signed in as you.

00:38.500 --> 00:45.124
And it's live, under your name. Every page shows its version, its source, and a way to report it.

00:47.700 --> 00:52.116
Each space is a git branch. Publish again, and you get a new version.

00:53.500 --> 00:59.404
Explainers, maps of tools, launch notes. All free, all public.

01:01.000 --> 01:04.000
Get started at pages dot flisk dot s i.
